detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — is it to maximize total profit (unit price minus raw material cost minus operating costs, with the operating cost charged proportionally to the fraction of each machine's capacity used), or is it to maximize total revenue, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options within one sentence."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any demand limits or minimum production requirements for the three products, or can the factory produce and sell any quantity of each product as long as machine capacity allows?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the existence of demand limits or minimum production requirements versus unlimited production within capacity."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the fixed operating cost of each machine, is the charge triggered by any positive amount of processing time on that machine (i.e., if even one unit is processed there, the full fixed cost applies), or is there some minimum utilization threshold below which the machine is considered not used?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding how the fixed cost is triggered (any usage vs. threshold), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since each product must go through both procedure A and procedure B, is the quantity of each product that enters procedure A required to equal the quantity that completes procedure B (i.e., no work-in-progress or leftover units allowed), so that the number of finished units of each product is the same whether counted at procedure A or procedure B?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking whether flow balance is required between the two procedures, with no other independent requests."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is this raw material cost incurred for every unit that enters production (i.e., for every finished unit of that product)?",
    "Is it the only variable cost besides the fixed machine operating costs?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains two semantically independent questions: one asking about the timing/trigger of the cost (per unit entering production) and another asking about the exclusivity of the cost (whether it is the only variable cost besides fixed machine costs)."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The \"Effective Machine Hours\" for each machine (e.g., 6000 for A1, 10000 for A2) — is this the total available processing time for that machine over the entire planning period, so the sum of processing times for all products assigned to that machine must not exceed this number?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the definition and constraint implication of 'Effective Machine Hours'."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The processing times in the table (e.g., 5 for Product I on A1, 7 for Product I on A2) — are these the processing times per unit of product on that machine, so that the total time on a machine is the sum over products of (units produced × per-unit time)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the interpretation of the processing time values."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the fixed operating cost is triggered by any positive use of a machine, and there is no demand limit, is it acceptable for the model to leave a machine completely unused (zero units processed, no fixed cost charged) if that is more profitable than using it?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy decision on whether machines can be left unused to avoid fixed costs."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product I, which can be processed on A1 or A2 for procedure A and on B1, B2, or B3 for procedure B — is it allowed for the units of Product I to be split across different machines within a procedure (e.g., some units of Product I on A1 and some on A2), or must all units of a given product use a single machine per procedure?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether production units can be split across machines or must be assigned to a single machine per procedure."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The unit prices (1.25, 2.00, 2.80 yuan) — is the revenue for each product simply the number of finished units multiplied by its unit price, with no other revenue or cost components?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the revenue calculation method and the absence of other components."
}
